Align mixed target/draft attention pages by logical block size.

This patch is opt-in with VLLM_ALIGN_HETEROGENEOUS_ATTN_PAGES=1. It runs before
the normal one-pass page unifier and grows natural attention pages to a fixed
point in their shared kernel-block granularity. It does not change KV storage,
block tables, scheduler semantics, or Mamba padding.

On the CMP 170HX Qwen3.8 target-FP8/draft-BF16 configuration, the stock path
first creates target=880 and draft=448 token blocks, then pads the target's
1,802,240-byte page to the draft's 1,835,008 bytes. Worker reshape cannot
represent the periodic padding gap with one affine virtual-block stride. The
fixed-point alignment instead produces target=896 and draft=448, whose natural
pages are both exactly 1,835,008 bytes, so backend 16-token blocks remain
contiguous and no Worker reshape shim is required.

Apply before spec-decode-fp8-kv-sm80.patch.

Written against the repository's vLLM 0.27.1 patch stack.

